Description: R package for BADGERS (Bayesian ADaptive Graph-guided
    Errors-in-variables Regression Solution), a graph-guided Bayesian
    regression model for high-dimensional data with replicated covariates and
    measurement error. Latent covariates are inferred from replicate
    measurements, which may differ in number across predictors, and a
    working graph links the predictor-specific shrinkage parameters through a
    constrained Wishart prior. It provides an Rcpp-based Markov chain Monte
    Carlo sampler, tuning of the log-shrinkage mean and scale (mu, nu), and
    optionally the precision penalty parameter psi, over a grid using the
    validation mean squared prediction error, and simulation utilities for
    generating data with a true or noisy working graph.
